  "id": "COMPOUND:17776 - PROTEIN:5776",
  "verbalization": "Lobelanidin exhibits a consistent relationship with MIP, as evidenced by its ability to target multiple cell lines, including HepG2, LNCaP, and H9, all of which are implicated in the expression of the compound. The compound is identified as a target of these cell lines, suggesting a potential mechanism of action that involves the regulation of these cellular pathways. The presence of a common structural motif in all three targets—(1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol—indicates a possible common mechanism of action, possibly involving the modulation of cellular processes such as proliferation or survival. The evidence suggests that Lobelanidin may act through a mechanism that involves the inhibition or regulation of these pathways, with the compound potentially acting as a modulator of cellular responses in these cell lines. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Lobelanidin may interact with MIP through a mechanism that is not yet fully understood, but is likely to involve the regulation of cellular processes associated with these targets.",
